# 6.7.13 (D11 (a), the user 2026-10-15): the reading kept — an untyped value is the struct's word, at most 8
# bytes; a struct over 8 B keeps the rest. The filed repro verbatim (its `main` as dw_main):
# issues/2026-10-14-untyped-store-through-struct-pointer-over-8-bytes-reading.md — 72 (70 would be the
# zero-extended reading the user declined).
